 "about": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex, nofollow\"><meta name=\"referrer\" content=\"no-referrer\">\n<title>About this signing page · Shōkai</title><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\"></head>\n<body><main class=\"about\">\n<h1>About this signing page</h1>\n<div class=\"notice\">\n<p><strong>This signing page is an early, test-stage convenience.</strong> Shōkai is still a draft, and Kigenka runs this page while it's being tested.</p>\n<p>Your passkey stays on your phone or computer. Kigenka never sees it and can't sign for you.</p>\n<p>A passkey works only on the web address it was made on, here <strong>{{RP_ID}}</strong>. We plan to keep this address. If it ever has to change, we'll tell you at least {{NOTICE_DAYS}} days in advance. A way to sign a move to a new key with the passkey you have now, so the places that know your representative can keep recognizing it, is planned (proposal P24, for v0.4) but doesn't exist yet; we won't move the address before it does.</p>\n<p>Everything you've already signed stays valid either way.</p>\n<p>You don't have to use this page. Anyone can sign with their own signing page or their own key; see \"Signing on your own\" below.</p>\n</div>\n<h2>What if the signing page's address changes?</h2>\n<p>{{RP_ID}} is an early, test-stage convenience run by Kigenka while Shōkai is a draft. A passkey works only on the web address it was made on, so we intend to keep this address. If it ever has to move, owners will be told at least {{NOTICE_DAYS}} days in advance, on this page, on the Shōkai site and in the repository, and given a way to move to a new key, signed with their current one, before the old address stops signing. That way is planned (proposal P24, for v0.4) and doesn't exist yet; the address won't move before it does. Everything already signed stays valid.</p>\n<h2>What we never promise</h2>\n<p>An uptime, a date, or that a move needs nothing from you.</p>\n<h2>Signing on your own</h2>\n<p>Run the reference signing page on your own domain and register your passkey there, or, for an organization, sign with a key published at your own domain (<code>did:web</code>). Places check every owner signature the same way, whatever page made it; this page gets no special treatment.</p>\n<p><a href=\"./\">Back to signing</a></p>\n</main></body></html>\n"
